{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall make poles for the altar, poles of acacia wood.</b> It should have said ועשית בדים למזבח עצי שטים, or it should have said ועשית למזבח בדי עצי שטים, as it said regarding the ark and likewise regarding the table: והבאת את הבדים בטבעות. And the reason it needed the lengthiness of expression regarding the poles is to allude to what is written (II Chronicles 5:9): ״ויאריכו הבדים״ — 'and the poles were long' — which was a miraculous deed, as the Sages, of blessed memory, mentioned: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: the poles are destined to lengthen for 480 years from the exodus of the children of Israel from Egypt, as it is said: ״ויאריכו הבדים״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The phrase תפ\"ז appears to be a typographical or manuscript corruption for ת\"פ (480), the traditional figure for the span from the Exodus to the building of Solomon's Temple in II Chronicles 5:9; rendered literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:52.451613906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}